  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The permission hereby granted shall be for a limited period , the period being two years from the date of this decision when the use shall cease and any approved structures and associated paraphernalia shall be removed and the land restored to its former condition, within two months of this permission expiring, as set out in the note below.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [Covering letter dated 29 April 2021; 1654-PL1/04 A; 1654-PL1/01 B and Preliminary Ecological Appraisal. Received: 30 April 2021. Design and Access Statement Revision 2 12 November 2021 and 1654-PL1/03 D. Received: 15 November 2021].",
    "Condition : 3 - The trees that are specified on the drawings hereby approved to be retained shall be protected throughout the course of the development by methods that conform to the best practice guidance contained in British Standard BS5837: 2012 or any guidance that shall have superseded it.",
    "Condition : 4 - The hereby approved use shall not operate outside of the following hours; 6am- 8.30pm Monday to Sunday term time and 7am-8.30pm Monday to Sunday during school holidays.",
    "Condition : 5 - Access to the slipway south of the site shall not at any time be restricted or obstructed. Any equipment associated with the approved use shall be managed appropriately to ensure no obstructions are caused for other users.",
    "Condition : 6 - Within three months of the date of this permission, the applicant shall have entered into an agreement with Brentford Voice to provide a financial contribution towards installing an interpretive panel for the ?Brentford Waterside Heritage Trail? close to the site.",
    "Condition : 7 - The ?introduced shrubs? around the site as detailed within the submitted Preliminary Ecological Appraisal dated April 2021 shall be retained and maintained for the duration of the permission. Should any shrubs be damaged then a suitable replacement shall be planted within the next planting season."
  ],
